libgccjit: build against libc++ and export the new entry points on Darwin

jit-playback.h and jit-target.h include <vector> and <unordered_set>,
which with macOS's libc++ pull in <locale>; after system.h has defined
_() and poisoned names, that header no longer parses.  The jit sources
and config/default-jit.cc ask system.h for <vector> instead, as the rest
of GCC does with INCLUDE_VECTOR.  jit-target.h hashed C strings with
std::_Hash_bytes, which only libstdc++ has; libiberty's
htab_hash_string does the same job.  Darwin links the library with
libgccjit.exports, not libgccjit.map, and the fork added its entry
points only to the map.

